+### Opt-in keys
+
+Client configs may set (defaults in `configs/defaults.yaml` are the historical behaviour): `queues`,
+`calendar_grid` (grid from the calendar, DST-aware), `queue_hours`, `apply_occupancy_cap`,
+`attainment_intervals: operating`, `scheduler: weekly` with `max_hours_ratio`, `min_rest_hours`,
+`split_contracts` and `break_rule: surplus`, and `sow_reports`. Northwind's file shows them in use.
+`scheduler: weekly` plans on coverage net of breaks and enforces rest, split-shift eligibility and the break
+rule while scheduling; with it the evaluator audits those rules too (`rest`, `split_shift`, `break_*` keys in
+`violations`). An export with a `utc_offset` column is converted with that offset.
+
